      "writtenOn": "2017-08-30T00:38:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh ok you\u0027re referring to the combination of tick gran. and the CPU going stale. Yeah I guess that would cause a drop in the middle of the window.. I understand the hysteresis point but if its not expensive to change the frequency back up when needed, then its probably not that big of a deal?\nPELT also would have this issue, kind of, right? So we\u0027re not doing any more worse with WALT than we would be if we were using PELT. I think another way to look at it is to let the governor decide about whether it wants to drop the frequency or not than enforcing the behavior that WALT wants.\nAlso I was thinking - how does the remote update stuff relate to this patch? I think that came up on today\u0027s call but it was early in the morning for me and I hadn\u0027t had my coffee yet. (Also sorry for my verbosity)",
      "parentUuid": "07ec2b7c_7e940048",
      "revId": "f66ce011c923cb565f12cd223e2fe2ddf6650e50",
